# Classes below a class declare a private field, a private method and a private accessor. Their objects, and those of the classes below them, are allocated in `round`,
# with room for the private fields, and the initializers and methods are called directly. No private name is defined, read or stored by the run time, but for one way
# out of `#next`: the objects leave the program in `answer`, and `tick` hands its receiver on to `#next`, so that may be another object than one of these.
